# AI-native GCC plugin policy file.
#
# Grammar (one rule per line; '#' starts a comment):
#
#   disable_pass=<pass>
#   disable_pass=<pass> if <feature><op><value>[&&<feature><op><value>]...
#
# <feature>  : basic_blocks | gimple_statements | phi_nodes | calls |
#              branches | edges | memory_reads | memory_writes | float_ops
# <op>       : <=  >=  ==  !=  <  >
# <value>    : integer
#
# Unconditional rules disable a pass for every function in the translation
# unit. Conditional rules are evaluated against per-function IR features
# captured after SSA construction, so they only affect passes that run
# later for that function. Malformed lines abort compilation with a
# diagnostic instead of being silently ignored. Passes are never
# force-enabled because their compiler prerequisites may not hold.
#
# Examples:
#
# disable_pass=evrp
# disable_pass=ccp if gimple_statements<50&&basic_blocks<10
# disable_pass=cddce if memory_writes>=8
